   "text": "Messaging: contrast, strength and reassurance rather than attraction",
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "These five documents show what officials told themselves the message was for, from 1949 to 1969. The thread is that the message was built from the audience's fears and loyalties, anti-communism, neutralism and doubt about American strength, and never from the appeal of American society alone."
  },
  {
   "kind": "document",
