   "documentId": "d386",
   "notes": [
    "Agent run f11, 2026-10-31: Jessup, November 1949: a larger information program in non-Communist Asia is wanted to show sympathy with nationalism and to expose Soviet imperialism, with the US and the USSR contrasted by the record."
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "excerpt",
   "volumeId": "frus1949v07p2",
   "documentId": "d386",
   "text": "A considerably expanded information program both in Communist and non-Communist areas of Asia is called for, both to demonstrate our understanding and sympathy for the nationalist aspirations of the Asian peoples and to expose the menace to these aspirations created by Soviet imperialism. No opportunity should be lost to contrast—by reference to the record—the aims and attitudes of the US and the USSR."
  },
  {
   "kind": "document",
   "volumeId": "frus1952-54v12p2",
   "documentId": "d403",
   "notes": [
    "Agent run f11, 2026-10-31: Psychological Strategy Board plan for Thailand, September 1953: information work is to run through local leaders and local outlets, alongside aid and paramilitary preparation. Image work is one instrument among several."
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "excerpt",
   "volumeId": "frus1952-54v12p2",
   "documentId": "d403",
   "text": "In projecting U.S. leadership, however, we must work with and through indigenous leadership wherever possible."
  },
  {
   "kind": "document",
   "volumeId": "frus1955-57v09",
   "documentId": "d189",
   "notes": [
