   "text": "What officials believed about the Asian audience",
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "These four documents are where policymakers say, in their own words, what kind of people they thought they were addressing. The thread is a mix of respect for nationalism and distance from the audience: poor and apathetic, wary of whites, persuaded by their own countrymen, or emotionally pacifist."
  },
